  ('13e293b2-6350-5d24-91e3-0fb4cef80be1', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-word-parts'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The prefix ex- means "out," and ped means "foot," so the word first meant freeing someone's feet. What did the city do "To expedite the final stage"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It postponed the work until after the school year","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"It inspected the work to check for problems","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"It sped up the work by adding a second crew","is_correct":true},{"text":"It lowered the cost by using fewer workers","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It sped up the work by adding a second crew$q$, $q$To expedite is to free up and speed along, and hiring a second crew let the bridge open "three weeks ahead of schedule." Using fewer workers contradicts the passage, which says the city hired more.$q$, 'draft', '561426fe-8037-5ada-8121-ba0a8b7ad0a4')
