   $q$The Greek prefix pseudo- means "false," and the root nym means "name." What is a "pseudonym"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A short summary printed on the back of a book","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"The real name printed on an author's birth record","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"A poor review written about an author's first book","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-nearby-detail"},{"text":"An invented name an author uses instead of a real one","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$An invented name an author uses instead of a real one$q$, $q$Pseudo- plus nym means "false name," and the passage restates it as "pen name" and "invented names." A poor review is mentioned as one reason for using a pen name, not as its meaning.$q$, 'draft', 'd0803843-f475-5e37-85c5-18ed26350bae')
