   $q$The Latin root ver means "true," and the suffix -ify means "to make." What does Wen want Imani to do when he says "Then verify it"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Rewrite the article in a shorter form","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-nearby-detail"},{"text":"Remove the numbers from the article","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Report the numbers just as she was told","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Check whether the numbers are actually true","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Check whether the numbers are actually true$q$, $q$To verify is "to make sure something is true," and Wen tells her to call the business office to check the numbers. Reporting what she was told without checking is the opposite of verifying.$q$, 'draft', '5a67b95b-ebcb-5bb8-9b9d-986e52e1e701')
