   $q$The prefix re- can mean "back," and duc means "lead," so to reduce is to lead something back to a smaller amount. What does it mean that the terrace design "greatly reduces erosion"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They make much less soil wash away","is_correct":true},{"text":"They stop all rain from reaching the soil","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-claim"},{"text":"They cause much more soil to wash away","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"They move the lost soil back uphill","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They make much less soil wash away$q$, $q$To reduce is to make smaller, and the passage explains that rain "pauses on each level and soaks in" instead of carrying soil away. Moving soil back uphill takes "lead back" too literally; the word means lessening the loss.$q$, 'draft', '1c3ac066-7dd6-5e4a-94b3-da82b7156735')
