   $q$What is the central claim of this argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Delmont University should study how roof color affects city temperatures.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The council should require reflective white coatings on all flat downtown roofs.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Marlow Falls recorded more hot days last July than in any earlier summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mistakes-evidence-for-claim"},{"text":"Property owners should receive grants to replace their old tar roofs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The council should require reflective white coatings on all flat downtown roofs.$q$, $q$The first paragraph ends with the claim that the council "should require that every flat roof downtown be coated with reflective white paint within five years." The record heat is evidence that sets up the problem, not the claim itself.$q$, 'draft', 'd9176f60-6879-5e74-bee5-83307ea28e8d')
