-- Passage rg11-argument-evidence-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('90e73931-c64f-5ecc-9c33-a6e38b1661ef', 'rg11-argument-evidence-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-argument-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Our Fields Deserve Turf$q$, $q$The grass fields at Westbrook High School are a disgrace. After every rainstorm, the soccer field turns to mud, and last October three home games had to be moved or canceled. The school board should replace both the soccer and baseball fields with artificial turf before next season.

Turf is playable in almost any weather. Riverton High, two towns over, installed turf four years ago and has not canceled a single game because of field conditions since. Our athletes deserve the same reliability.

Turf also saves money over time. According to the district's facilities office, maintaining the grass fields costs about $48,000 a year for mowing, watering, fertilizing and reseeding. A turf field needs only occasional grooming. Although installation would cost roughly $1.1 million for both fields, the savings would add up year after year.

Some parents have raised concerns that turf surfaces get much hotter than grass on sunny days and may lead to more of certain injuries. My own daughter has played on turf at tournaments for years, and she has never been hurt, so I find these concerns overblown.

Others say the money should go to repairing the leaking roof in the science wing. But if we keep putting off investments in athletics, our best players will transfer to schools that care about sports, and Westbrook will never field a winning team again. Either we commit to our athletes now, or we accept being a school with no athletic program worth the name.

Every coach I asked at last week's booster club meeting supports turf. The board should listen to the people who know our teams best and approve this project.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
