  ('1da534fb-401b-5e09-8fd1-562d6efde6ea', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-authors-purpose'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Why does the speaker begin three sentences in a row with "Maybe" in the first paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The repetition shows that she is uncertain whether anyone will ever read code, which weakens her later advice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"The repetition imitates the way computer programs check conditions, which shows her technical expertise.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The repetition piles up possible readers, making an abstract idea concrete and building to the surprise that it could be the listener.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The repetition lists the three rules for clear code in order, which she explains in detail in the fourth paragraph.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The repetition piles up possible readers, making an abstract idea concrete and building to the surprise that it could be the listener.$q$, $q$Each "Maybe" adds a new kind of reader, and the third saves the most surprising one, "it is you," for last. She is certain someone will read the code; the "Maybe" is about who, not whether.$q$, 'draft', '2be6111b-32d2-5cbc-9ffb-f2ed8c24afa7')
