   $q$What are the two main purposes of the speech?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To explain how thermometers work and to sell new weather instruments","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To describe a famous blizzard and to warn listeners about dangerous storms","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"To criticize satellites and to call for an end to automated sensors","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"To honor Eleanor's long service and to recruit new volunteer observers","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To honor Eleanor's long service and to recruit new volunteer observers$q$, $q$The speech celebrates Eleanor's fifty-two years and ends with "consider taking up the pencil," an invitation to volunteer. He calls satellites "wonderful tools," so he is not attacking them.$q$, 'draft', '81b91a97-1acd-5d90-9d86-ab6197b94f24')
