  ('3da42468-a0c5-56d4-a549-a851a1cbfbd8', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-authors-purpose'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Why does the speaker mention Eleanor's birthday, her daughter's wedding, and the kitchen pot?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To show that the weather was unusually severe that year, which is the main subject of the speech","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"To show that she owned poor equipment, which proves that the weather service should have paid her","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-anecdote"},{"text":"To show that her family life was difficult, which explains why she found comfort in measuring weather","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To show her unbroken consistency, which he later argues is what gives her record its scientific value","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To show her unbroken consistency, which he later argues is what gives her record its scientific value$q$, $q$These details prove she never skipped a day, and he later says "A long record is only as valuable as its consistency." The kitchen pot shows determination in a blizzard, not a complaint about her equipment.$q$, 'draft', '81b91a97-1acd-5d90-9d86-ab6197b94f24')
