   $q$Why does the speaker discuss satellites and automated sensors in the fourth paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To suggest that Eleanor's notebooks should be replaced, by showing that modern machines make human observers unnecessary","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-concession"},{"text":"To answer the likely objection that volunteers are no longer needed, by noting machines' short history and frequent changes","is_correct":true},{"text":"To explain how satellites are built and launched, by describing the instruments they use to measure snow","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"To argue that satellites collect less data than volunteers, by comparing a single hour of machine data to Eleanor's notebooks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To answer the likely objection that volunteers are no longer needed, by noting machines' short history and frequent changes$q$, $q$He grants that machines gather huge amounts of data, then notes they have "existed for only a fraction of the time" and get "replaced, upgraded, and moved." He says they collect more data, not less, so the second choice reverses his words.$q$, 'draft', '81b91a97-1acd-5d90-9d86-ab6197b94f24')
