  ('d6684cdd-652e-583c-bdf6-b634fc82b927', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-authors-purpose'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How does the final paragraph make the speaker's request especially persuasive?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It threatens that the plan will fail without benches, and the word \"generous\" suggests that the committee has been selfish so far.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"It sets a tiny cost against a large human benefit, and the word \"generous\" casts the benches as a gift that reflects well on the committee.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It reveals for the first time that the benches are free, and the word \"generous\" thanks a donor who has already paid for them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It lists the exact price of each bench, and the word \"generous\" refers to the large size of the benches she has chosen.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It sets a tiny cost against a large human benefit, and the word "generous" casts the benches as a gift that reflects well on the committee.$q$, $q$"Less than one percent" makes the request seem easy, and calling it "the most generous thing in the entire plan" gives it moral weight the committee can take credit for. She states a cost, so the benches are not free, and her tone is inviting rather than threatening.$q$, 'draft', '4b8fd98d-207e-59f4-8602-08897cb27068')
