   $q$How does the speaker change over the course of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"From someone who admires the old observer to someone who rejects her advice entirely.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"From a confident expert to a nervous beginner who no longer trusts any instrument.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-change"},{"text":"The speaker does not change; each stanza simply records new weather in the same way.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"From an unsure newcomer copying the old observer to a confident one adding a lesson of their own.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$From an unsure newcomer copying the old observer to a confident one adding a lesson of their own.$q$, $q$Early on the speaker copies her numbers and sounds "younger than I want it to"; later the speaker writes a new line, "Then trust yourself for listening." That line extends her advice rather than rejecting it.$q$, 'draft', '9a4ef88a-55cf-58b8-9a48-a0854965e798')
