   $q$Why does the author place the lines "She knew almost no one by face. She knew nearly everyone by voice" before the call comes in?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They reveal that Hattie has worked the switchboard for many years in town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They establish the knowledge Hattie later uses to track down the doctor.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They explain why Hattie fails to recognize Lucia's voice on the line.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They show that Hattie dislikes the people of Marrow Creek and avoids them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They establish the knowledge Hattie later uses to track down the doctor.$q$, $q$Placed early, the lines prepare for the turning point, when her memory of the doctor's calls lets her find him. She has lived there only four months, so she is not a longtime operator.$q$, 'draft', '1a9e65b8-39e1-50b6-902a-f3c8c4deb422')
