   $q$How is Osei characterized at the beginning of the fable?$q$, $q$[{"text":"As shy and uncertain, rarely willing to share what he has measured.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"As jealous of the ducks, who know the river better than he does.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"As proud and sure of himself, happy to accept the title of Riverkeeper.","is_correct":true},{"text":"As careless about the river, never bothering to measure its depth.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$As proud and sure of himself, happy to accept the title of Riverkeeper.$q$, $q$Osei "prided himself" on his knowledge and "did not correct" the ducks who called him Riverkeeper. He does measure every morning, so he is not careless in the beginning, only overconfident.$q$, 'draft', '55ebc6fd-66db-5ce8-b1af-b853af85f1cf')
