   $q$Why does the author include the paragraph explaining that the pool dries up by July?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the pool is not important, since it disappears for half the year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"It describes the fish that live in the pool and compete with the salamanders.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It explains why Dao and Dr. Asante must finish their count before the sun comes up.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"It shows why salamanders depend on this fragile place, raising the stakes of the falling count.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows why salamanders depend on this fragile place, raising the stakes of the falling count.$q$, $q$The pool's drying is "exactly why spotted salamanders chose it," since no fish survive there, so the setting is essential to the species. The text says no fish live there, so they cannot be competitors.$q$, 'draft', '336999ff-fe0f-5352-98d3-9a8e128be4d7')
