   $q$Read together, what fuller picture of the period's change do the two texts offer than either text alone?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Progress was welcomed by young people and opposed by old people, who refused to admit any of its benefits.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Progress happened so slowly that people in the valley barely noticed it during their lifetimes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Progress brought real gains for many people while ending older ways of working that some tried to preserve in memory.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Progress mattered mostly to printers and readers, since books were the main cargo the railway carried.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Progress brought real gains for many people while ending older ways of working that some tried to preserve in memory.$q$, $q$Text 1 shows the gains, and Text 2 shows a lost trade along with Silas's wish that "somebody should remember how it was done." Silas openly admits a benefit, so the choice saying older people refused to see any is wrong.$q$, 'draft', '2cbfa2e0-a6cf-58c2-83c9-acab8782d163')
