   $q$What topic do both texts share?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The rules a town passed to keep bicycles off its main roads.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The popularity of the bicycle and the freedom of riding one.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The dangers of steep hills for horses pulling heavy wagons.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The complaints of shopkeepers about quiet business on Main Street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The popularity of the bicycle and the freedom of riding one.$q$, $q$The column describes the town's "bicycle fever" and the writer's own ride, and the poem celebrates going anywhere on "two wheels." The shopkeepers' complaints are only one detail in Text 1.$q$, 'draft', '4e2a7710-3c30-5026-9fce-daa8a90a602a')
