values
  ('4cb1e4eb-8039-54ae-a739-50db37eac9dd', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-comparing-texts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Both texts mention people who doubt the bicycle. How do the texts treat these doubts?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Both agree with the doubters and conclude that riding is unwise.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"Text 1 ignores the doubters, while Text 2 lets them have the final word.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Both show the doubters changing their minds after trying a bicycle.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Both record the doubts but let the experience of riding outweigh them.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Both record the doubts but let the experience of riding outweigh them.$q$, $q$The shopkeepers, the stable owner, the mother and the uncle all object, but the columnist's ride and the speaker's daily trips win out. Only the columnist himself is shown trying a bicycle; the mother and uncle never do.$q$, 'draft', '4e2a7710-3c30-5026-9fce-daa8a90a602a')
