   $q$How does the form of each text shape what it emphasizes about the bicycle?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The column focuses only on the writer's private feelings, while the poem reports the views of shopkeepers, doctors and stable owners in town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"},{"text":"The column uses rhyme to make its arguments memorable, while the poem uses plain paragraphs to give readers practical facts about riding.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-form"},{"text":"Both forms lead to the same emphasis, because a newspaper column and a poem must cover a topic in exactly the same way.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-form"},{"text":"The column surveys the bicycle's effects on many townspeople before a personal anecdote, while the rhymed poem stays inside one rider's widening world.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The column surveys the bicycle's effects on many townspeople before a personal anecdote, while the rhymed poem stays inside one rider's widening world.$q$, $q$As a column, Text 1 reports on shopkeepers, the stable owner and the doctor for a public audience before turning to the writer's ride, while the poem's rhymed first person tracks one rider's world growing "wide." The column is prose, not rhyme.$q$, 'draft', '4e2a7710-3c30-5026-9fce-daa8a90a602a')
