  ('f240784d-8a4c-52c1-85b6-86882b93dd08', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-comparing-texts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$How do the settings shape each text's treatment of the radio?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Both settings are crowded city buildings, so the radio plays the same role of entertaining strangers in each text.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-setting"},{"text":"On the remote farm the radio bridges distance from the outside world, while in the city it bridges the distance between neighbors living side by side.","is_correct":true},{"text":"On the farm the radio separates the family members from one another, while in the city it connects tenants who already knew each other well.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"On the farm the radio is used only for sports, while in the city it is used only for weather reports and concerts.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$On the remote farm the radio bridges distance from the outside world, while in the city it bridges the distance between neighbors living side by side.$q$, $q$The farm is "eleven miles away by muddy road" from town, while the tenants live close together yet know one another only "by the sound of their footsteps." The city tenants were strangers, not old friends.$q$, 'draft', '9d8c393f-48bf-5db3-a6a5-09caa47c9f27')
