   $q$In what way are Grandfather Anton in Text 1 and the quiet woman from the top floor in Text 2 alike?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Each refuses to listen to the radio and leaves before the broadcast ends.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Each owns the radio and decides when the others are allowed to listen to it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-characters"},{"text":"Each starts out apart from the others and is drawn in by what the radio offers.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Each explains how the radio works to the younger people who are listening.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Each starts out apart from the others and is drawn in by what the radio offers.$q$, $q$Anton declares that a box "could not possibly talk" yet asks to hear it again, and the woman who only said good morning joins the crowd on the stairs. Neither owns the radio; Papa and Mr. Dasgupta do.$q$, 'draft', '9d8c393f-48bf-5db3-a6a5-09caa47c9f27')
