   $q$How do the two forms express the shared theme in different ways?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The story builds hope from concrete evidence like buckets, damp soil and height marks, while the poem states hope as a personal promise that does not depend on proof.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The story uses rhyme and repeated stanzas, while the poem uses paragraphs and a narrator who follows a family.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-form"},{"text":"The story states hope as a promise without evidence, while the poem lists measurements and dates to prove the trees are growing taller.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"},{"text":"Both forms rely mainly on dialogue between the planter and the county man to explain how windbreaks work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-form"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The story builds hope from concrete evidence like buckets, damp soil and height marks, while the poem states hope as a personal promise that does not depend on proof.$q$, $q$Text 1 shows hope through things Nadia can see and touch ("the marks climbed a little higher"), while the poem ends with "a promise made in small green leaves / Is still a promise kept," a commitment made regardless of proof. The poem includes no measurements.$q$, 'draft', '10e9d0cb-9c22-509a-b6de-4a81b532ed66')
