   $q$Both texts describe someone looking at the moon after the landing. How do their thoughts differ?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Both characters lose interest in the moon at once, since it looks exactly as it always has to each of them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Tomasz worries the astronauts will not return, while the speaker feels certain the landing was only a story on the radio.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Tomasz turns back to imagine his town as seen from space, while the speaker searches the sky for a speck he cannot see.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"},{"text":"Tomasz looks outward, amazed that someone is up there, while the speaker turns back to imagine Earth and home as seen from the moon.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Tomasz looks outward, amazed that someone is up there, while the speaker turns back to imagine Earth and home as seen from the moon.$q$, $q$Tomasz tries "to spot a speck that he knew he could never see," while the speaker says "what struck me most was not the moon" but the thought of "this small blue place" seen from above. Both note the moon looks ordinary, but neither loses interest.$q$, 'draft', '6ebe01bc-a726-5127-b68d-6177561a23f1')
