  ('d17045b4-6a1e-53f9-82fa-2407d5ffdbba', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-connections'), null, 'medium',
   $q$How does the author connect the faster loading of ships to the number of ships coming to Calloway?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Because ships could leave in a day instead of a week, companies sent more vessels there.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Because more ships arrived, the port was forced to find a faster way to load them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"Because cargo was sealed, companies chose smaller ships that could visit more often.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Because cranes replaced workers, ships had to wait longer for a free berth at the pier.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because ships could leave in a day instead of a week, companies sent more vessels there.$q$, $q$Paragraph 4 states that a ship "could now leave in a day, so shipping companies began sending more vessels." The faster loading caused the increase; the passage never says more ships arrived first and forced the change.$q$, 'draft', '1097d629-e255-5598-b986-4dde68f333d1')
