   $q$How does Ellery's view in the final paragraph develop the ideas presented earlier in the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shifts the focus away from the mussels and blames the anglers for the lake's changing fish population.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It introduces a plan to remove every mussel so that Lake Oriel can return to its earlier condition.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It confirms the residents' first reaction that clearer water meant the lake had become healthier overall.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It recasts the clear water as one link in a wider chain of change and turns the goal toward prevention in other lakes.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It recasts the clear water as one link in a wider chain of change and turns the goal toward prevention in other lakes.$q$, $q$Calling Oriel "a different lake rather than a cleaner one" reframes the clear water as part of a chain affecting plants and fish, and the reports say removal is not possible, so the goal is preventing the chain elsewhere. The residents' first delight is exactly what this view corrects.$q$, 'draft', '5e1f05ff-2f43-5931-b1ba-93816a7e3c3c')
