   $q$Which statement best describes how the spoken introductions develop over the course of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They begin as a fix for distracted public audiences, move into the hall to welcome newcomers, and are adjusted until most listeners accept them.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They remain a minor detail that has no effect on the orchestra's audiences in either the neighborhood or the hall.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-emphasis"},{"text":"They begin as the director's main plan for the hall, fail in public spaces, and are finally dropped after subscribers complain about them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They begin as a request from longtime subscribers and are later copied by musicians performing in libraries and stations.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-sequence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They begin as a fix for distracted public audiences, move into the hall to welcome newcomers, and are adjusted until most listeners accept them.$q$, $q$The introductions start in paragraph 3 to hold distracted listeners, enter hall concerts "to welcome" new audiences in paragraph 4, and are shortened and accepted in paragraph 5. They were never dropped; the complaints faded instead.$q$, 'draft', 'fb7b5da7-5f6a-5c93-a4a1-7ed86632ecd3')
