   $q$In paragraph 5, what does it mean that Kwame "could conceive of" a future running his own workshop?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He remembered a workshop from his childhood.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-time-frame"},{"text":"He had already signed an agreement to open one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He felt nervous and wanted to avoid the idea.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"He could picture it in his mind as a real possibility.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He could picture it in his mind as a real possibility.$q$, $q$The idea "had seemed absurd" earlier but now feels "less like a fantasy and more like a destination he could actually reach," so to conceive of it is to imagine it as possible. Nothing suggests he has taken formal steps, so the signed agreement is unsupported.$q$, 'draft', '50aa5e60-24c7-592a-a197-dd2c65b9665e')
