   $q$In paragraph 2, critics call the project "a luxury no treasury could sustain." Which meaning of "sustain" fits this sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"to keep paying for over a long period","is_correct":true},{"text":"to confirm that something is true","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"other-meaning-of-word"},{"text":"to suffer or experience, as with an injury","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"other-meaning-of-word"},{"text":"to construct quickly and cheaply","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$to keep paying for over a long period$q$, $q$The sentence follows the point that building and staffing the towers "was also costly," so a treasury that cannot sustain the project cannot keep paying for it. "Suffer, as with an injury" is a real meaning of sustain, but a treasury does not suffer a luxury.$q$, 'draft', 'e2689ef4-27fd-53dc-9fbe-469045b5c079')
