   $q$In paragraph 3, many researchers are "more circumspect" than popular accounts. What does "circumspect" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"careful not to claim more than the evidence shows","is_correct":true},{"text":"eager to share exciting results quickly","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"interested mainly in the history of science","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unrelated-meaning"},{"text":"completely opposed to the research","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-restatement"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$careful not to claim more than the evidence shows$q$, $q$Unlike accounts that "quickly described" the networks, researchers point out what the evidence "does not prove," and paragraph 4 calls this "caution," so circumspect means careful about claims. Paragraph 4 also says the caution "is not a rejection," which rules out "completely opposed."$q$, 'draft', 'b93e6386-2a65-58ef-aefe-2334fd66785c')
