  ('902a8c8a-88d5-5dda-8690-3955421367da', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-context-clues'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In paragraph 3, researchers note that "results from one forest may not hold in another." Which meaning of "hold" fits this context?$q$, $q$[{"text":"to remain true or valid","is_correct":true},{"text":"to contain or store something","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"other-meaning-of-word"},{"text":"to delay or pause something","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"other-meaning-of-word"},{"text":"to grasp something in the hands","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$to remain true or valid$q$, $q$The sentence warns that a different forest with "different soil, species, or climate" might give different results, so "hold" means remain true. "Contain or store" is a real meaning of hold, but results are not being stored anywhere.$q$, 'draft', 'b93e6386-2a65-58ef-aefe-2334fd66785c')
