   $q$The solution was "pragmatic rather than elegant." Which sentence from the passage best clarifies the meaning of "pragmatic"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Each community set its clocks by the sun, declaring noon at the moment the sun stood highest overhead.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"\"Not everyone welcomed the change.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-paragraph-clue"},{"text":"\"Instead of insisting that every place follow the sun exactly, they divided large regions into broad zones, each one sharing a single standard time.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"\"The plan accepted a small inaccuracy in exchange for a large gain in order.\"","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"The plan accepted a small inaccuracy in exchange for a large gain in order."$q$, $q$Trading "a small inaccuracy" for "a large gain in order" shows the planners valued what works in practice over perfection, which is what pragmatic means. The sentence about dividing regions describes what they did, but not the practical tradeoff that defines the word, and the sentences "Not everyone welcomed the change" and "Each community set its clocks by the sun" come from other paragraphs and say nothing about the tradeoff.$q$, 'draft', '81c33a08-8435-5273-a480-ca2312ce12f4')
