  ('e996551c-004a-50e6-8362-29a90d2989db', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-figurative-language'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The author writes that "Imaginary islands proved remarkably stubborn." What does "stubborn" suggest about these islands?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sailors refused to believe that the islands existed at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"Mapmakers argued angrily with each other about the islands.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They stayed on maps for a long time and were hard to remove.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They were rocky places that were very difficult to land on.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They stayed on maps for a long time and were hard to remove.$q$, $q$Giving the islands a human trait, stubbornness, shows how they "could survive on charts for generations" despite never being seen. The islands were imaginary, so they had no real rocks for anyone to land on.$q$, 'draft', '785f8d37-79b3-5bda-9bc0-56a4f5a84eee')
