   $q$The author says scientists holding an ice core are "holding a frozen archive in their hands." What does "frozen archive" mean here?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A tool that measures how cold the ice sheet is","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"A stack of old paper files kept inside a freezer","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"A collection of photographs of frozen landscapes","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A preserved record of the past stored in the ice","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A preserved record of the past stored in the ice$q$, $q$An archive is a collection of records, and the passage explains that ice traps air, ash and chemical clues from the past. The ice itself is the record, so a literal stack of paper files misses the metaphor.$q$, 'draft', '749dcbcc-aaba-5b63-9630-c346625f1c23')
