  ('a94ec63b-5c08-5ed9-a2e2-2fbb69e04141', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Henrik says, "You beat me by not doing anything," and Amara answers, "I did plenty. I just did it slowly." How does her reply respond to his statement?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She agrees that she made no real moves during the second half.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"She is offended and argues that she made many quick captures.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"She corrects his overstatement: her waiting was an active, patient plan.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She admits that she won mostly because Henrik made a lucky mistake.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She corrects his overstatement: her waiting was an active, patient plan.$q$, $q$Henrik's line exaggerates, but Amara's smile and "I just did it slowly" show that her rook shuffling was a deliberate strategy, not inaction. She is smiling, not offended, and she never claims quick captures.$q$, 'draft', '936952f3-ff9f-55d2-b339-31906970cce9')
