   $q$The author says embarrassing photos "resurface years later." What does "resurface" suggest that a word such as "appear" would not?$q$, $q$[{"text":"That the photos have been edited to look different from the original","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"That the photos are being seen by the public for the very first time","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-connotation"},{"text":"That the photos were taken near water and later rose to the top","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"That the photos come back after people thought they were buried and gone","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$That the photos come back after people thought they were buried and gone$q$, $q$"Resurface" suggests something rising again after being hidden, which fits the idea of an internet that does not let the past stay forgotten. "Appear" would be neutral and could mean a first showing, which misses the sense of return.$q$, 'draft', '2c939315-9602-56db-a4ae-170c85dba003')
